Conclusion:  Whip sucks even compared to pickaxe at the
same enchantment, and in the long run all weapons can be
enchanted up.  For the pickaxe, it's only the fact that
it is in the same weapon class as dwarvish mattock aka
broad pick.  That weapon is one of the hardest hitting
non-artifacts in the game and it is carried by plenty
of dwarves so the mines will supply at least one.  Even
better, both pickaxe and mattock can dig and that gets
more and more valuable as you get deeper.

> How do you deal with the low strength? Pushing boulders around is a
> massively boring activity that also tends to make your food supply run
> low.

Same as any other character.  Do what you can when you
can to incredase strength and eventually you'll make it
up to 18/**.  In the meantime dump stuff near the stairs
and maybe start building up a stash on some level.
Never go Burdened accept when shuttling stuff to your
stash and always be ready to drop enough to be Unburdened
when facing anything stronger than a newt.

> How is it that people tend to get their hands on silver sabres? I never
> seem to find any.

Patience.  The watch captain has 50-50 chance silver saber
or long sword.  Further down the same is true of the
captains that appear among soldiers.  There are usually
enough captains in the two castles that you're eventually
almost certain to have one.


